  "body": "## Highlights\n\n- **Share any pane.** One `Share` entry in every pane menu, or `Cmd+Shift+S` (`Ctrl+Shift+S` elsewhere), previews the pane as a picture, then posts it to a chat channel or copies a link. (#1703)\n- **Ask Gloom about any pane.** A small button beside `?`, the pane menu or `Alt+A` opens a new conversation with that pane attached. (#1690)\n- **A calmer reader.** Stories from `SRCH` and the news open with the headline and the gist, in short paragraphs without page clutter, and `n` and `p` step through results. (#1695)\n- **Chat that stays put.** The message list keeps your place, you can react with emoji in sync with Discord, and bots carry a badge. (#1701, #1693, #1706)\n- **Charts keep up.** Charts inside a pane follow a resize to the pixel, and `CMP` reads every series under the crosshair, pans without jumping and loads older bars as you pan back. (#1667, #1714, #1691)\n- **A closer `MAP`.** Zoom to a harbor, pan with the arrow keys, and see countries in proportion. (#1689)\n- **Perpetual markets everywhere.** Quote, search and list them like any other listing, with a stock's perpetual premium and funding in watchlists and portfolios. (#1698, #1660)\n\n## Also in this release\n\n- Exports name their units and end with their source and dates, and `CBR` exports carry a citation per row. (#1666, #1712)\n- A held shortcut runs once per press, and theme previews and new charts paint together. (#1694, #1692)\n- `OVDV` and `OMON` fit the skew when a chain has no open interest, and `HIVG` adds per-session 25-delta skew. (#1700, #1705)\n- Command line: tables fit a narrow `--width`, an unknown function name lists the closest ones, and `shot --strict` exits non-zero when a capture is unusable. (#1713, #1699)\n- Rates: find central banks and economic series by name, and read euro and rating high-yield spreads, CDX 1M moves and the EU carbon allowance auction price. (#1711, #1668, #1671)\n- Paste a list of symbols into a watchlist from the command bar. (#1687)\n\n[Full diff](https://github.com/gloom-sh/gloomberb/compare/v0.16.5...v0.16.6)\n"
}
